-- EXPECT-ERROR: refinement violation: argument `n` of `take_n` does not satisfy precondition
-- Refinement types (widening slice 12, §2.14). A DIRECT call to a function
-- whose parameter carries {T | pred} has its argument checked against pred
-- by the separate post-typecheck lib/refinecheck pass (NOT by typecheck.ml,
-- which erases the refinement to its base type -- see accept/t75's header).
-- `take_n(-3)` violates `_ >= 0` with a literal argument -- Z3 refutes it
-- (no path-sensitivity needed), so `--check` rejects with the pinned
-- "refinement violation" message. Accept companion: accept/t75 (satisfied).
mod M do
  needs IO.Console
  fn take_n(n : {Int | _ >= 0}) : Int do n end
  fn main() do
    println(int_to_string(take_n(-3)))
  end
end
